WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:02.710
- [Narrator] Driving today might feel like

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:04.350
you're using a tech gadget.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.970
Especially if it's a car developed

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.783
by Chinese automaker XPENG.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.570
First, you'll need your phone
to activate the features.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.476
- We need to scan it.

00:00:13.476 --> 00:00:14.309
(beep)

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:16.024
- [Narrator] Then you'll give commands.

00:00:16.024 --> 00:00:18.531
(woman speaking foreign language)

00:00:18.531 --> 00:00:21.005
(car replies in foreign language)

00:00:21.005 --> 00:00:22.070
- [Narrator] And when you
get to your destination

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:23.506
the vehicle will park itself.

00:00:23.506 --> 00:00:27.330
(car speaking foreign language)

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.210
- [Narrator] These features
are all part of XPENG's

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.430
strategy to stand out

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.210
in the world's second biggest
market for electric vehicles.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.720
The company is competing in China,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.190
not only with EV leaders like Tesla,

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.530
- [Man] The all electric, F-150 lightning.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.060
- [Narrator] But also
traditional automakers

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.240
like Ford and GM, which are doubling down

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.320
on producing electric vehicles too.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.480
- Technology, combined
with mobility and auto,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.510
is where we think the future is gonna be.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.430
- [Narrator] One high-tech feature

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.110
automakers are racing to build,

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.290
full self-driving capabilities.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:57.700
But putting more tech in vehicles

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.380
creates engineering challenges
and also risky behaviors.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.100
- She's totally asleep.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.580
- [Narrator] Like Tesla, XPENG is trying

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.510
to push the boundaries of
integrating tech into our cars,

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:11.130
and has gotten into a spat
with Elon Musk over software.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:11.963
(tech music)

00:01:11.963 --> 00:01:13.870
So we went to XPENG's, RND lab

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.690
to understand its vision for driving.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:18.990
- We are working on a very unique culture

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.920
and capability that allows
to rapidly innovate.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.169
We'll be able to be one of
the top players in China.

00:01:25.169 --> 00:01:28.100
(man speaking foreign language)

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.530
- [Narrator] XPENG has always operated

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.740
like a tech startup since
it was founded in 2014.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.830
- We have lot of the traditional
auto background employees.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.080
At the same time we have staff

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.510
coming from leading technology companies.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.940
- Brian Gu is a former
JP Morgan executive,

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.090
who took over as XPENG's vice chairman

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.930
and president in 2018.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:49.147
- We actually dedicate
close to 40% of our staff

00:01:49.147 --> 00:01:51.510
in the RND area in software.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.230
So I think that's very different compared

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:55.123
to traditional auto companies.

00:01:55.123 --> 00:01:56.400
(champion bell rings)

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.480
- [Narrator] Gu was the
man behind XPENG's IPO

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.250
on the New York stock exchange last year,

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.083
that raised $1.7 billion.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.690
Using this money, XPENG
hired more engineers

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:08.170
and poached talent from
China's top tech companies

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.883
like Tencent and Alibaba.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.460
And one of the big goals for
this larger engineering team

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.730
is to develop self-driving technology.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.627
Currently, XPENG offers what it calls,

00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:20.090
"Advanced driver assistance systems."

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.030
This controls the car on a highway,

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.660
but you have to keep your
hands on the steering wheel.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.140
In five years, XPENG's goal

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.170
is to develop a fully autonomous vehicle

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.330
that doesn't need anyone in the seat.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.240
To make this happen, it's invested a lot

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.890
in software and hardware.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.220
- We are keeping basically investment

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.780
in autonomous driving as
our number one priority.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:40.613
- [Narrator] Xinzhou Wu

00:02:40.613 --> 00:02:42.860
leads XPENG's autonomous driving division.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.210
Its software decides when
the car should accelerate

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.070
or brake, and that relies on information

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.800
that comes from a vast array of sensors.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.650
Plus, the most recent XPENG
cars are going to be equipped

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.010
with a special piece of
hardware called Lidar,

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:57.490
which uses light waves
to map what's around.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.790
- Lidar can do a range calculation

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:03.470
to get a kind of a 3D world view.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:06.940
Here we can make autonomous
driving in the city safer.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.150
- [Narrator] Lidar is expensive,

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.690
typically costing about a $1000 a piece.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.210
And XPENG's latest car will take two.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.850
The company will be the first automaker

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.640
to mass produce Lidar-equipped
vehicles this year.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.170
And its entry point will
be lower than $35,000.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:24.850
But XPENG's tech strategy
has some big detractors.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.403
- Lidar is, is a fool's
errand, expensive sensors,

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.310
that are unnecessary.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.090
- [Narrator] Tesla is
taking a different approach

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.680
and instead of investing in software

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.260
that can interpret what's on the road,

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.430
using only regular cameras.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.370
- Tesla has very much
tried to do self-driving

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.344
on the cheap with the bare
minimum number of sensors

00:03:46.344 --> 00:03:48.500
that they think they can get away with.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.640
- [Narrator] Sam Abuelsamid
is an auto analyst

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.320
who's been analyzing EV tech
features for the past 10 years.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:57.520
During a recent road test of
EV's self-driving capabilities,

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.940
Tesla came in first by a big margin.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.060
But Abuelsamid says XPENG's
system has more potential

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.410
because of its hardware.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.440
- With the right software, you
can do distance measurement,

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.800
but it's never going to be
as accurate or as reliable

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.730
as what you could do with
active sensors like Lidar.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.940
- [Narrator] A lot of sensors and cameras

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.890
potentially mean the self-driving software

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.930
is receiving more useful information

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.540
about what's on the road.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.780
Just compare XPENG's 32
sensors in its latest sedan,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.180
to the 12 sensors and 8
cameras in a Tesla vehicle.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.600
Tesla didn't respond to
a request for comment,

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.550
but Musk has tweeted several times

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.880
that its camera based system

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.900
is more precise than sensors like Lidar.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.530
But the Tesla and XPENG rivalry

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:40.460
goes beyond choice of hardware.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.490
It all came to a head when
Tesla filed a lawsuit in 2019

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.990
against one of its former
employees in the US,

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.210
who had quit to join XPENG.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.670
The lawsuit alleged that he
took copies of the source code

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.130
of Tesla's current
driver assistance system,

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.590
in order to hand it over
to his new employer.

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:58.360
In court documents, Tesla
alleged the Chinese company was

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.100
inspired by and on a
mission to beat Tesla.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.220
And has transparently imitated
Tesla's design, technology

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.900
and even its business model.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.620
In April, Tesla settled the lawsuit

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.950
with the former employee,

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.460
who acknowledged he shouldn't
have saved the source codes.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.880
But said he didn't provide it to XPENG.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.750
XPENG said the engineer no
longer works for the company

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.760
and that its in-house developed RND

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:21.160
has been its competitive advantage.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.640
- I view Tesla as our partner
rather than competitor.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.160
Tesla never brought that
claim against our company,

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.080
which means that there is no evidence

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.109
to point any wrongdoing.

00:05:33.109 --> 00:05:34.370
(car accelerating)

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.390
- [Narrator] But if there's one challenge

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.200
that the two rivals are facing together,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.450
it's the uphill battle
with the public perception

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.440
of their prized tech.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.910
- There's a growing sense that

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.880
the driver assistance
systems that they have,

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.090
the capabilities have been oversold.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.030
- [Narrator] Edward Niedermeyer
is an industry observer

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.910
who pushes for self-driving technology

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.970
as a way to make roads safer.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:57.640
- Okay Tesla, let's get this trip started.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.200
- [Narrator] But he
says social media videos

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.200
showing some drivers operating a Tesla

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.500
from the backseat, shows
how dangerous these systems

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.000
can be when people are
not using them properly.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.900
- There's considerable
research that shows us,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.850
people are much more likely
to misuse those systems

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.763
if they overestimate their capability.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.343
- [Narrator] Tesla has repeatedly said

00:06:15.343 --> 00:06:17.893
that features it offers
make driving safer.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.290
Meanwhile, XPENG is
working on a driver's test,

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:24.560
acknowledging that its self-driving
system has limitations.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.900
- For our drivers to be able to unlock

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.490
the autonomous driving features,

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.100
they actually need to take a test.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.340
We also need to educate the drivers

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.671
how to properly use those technologies.

00:06:34.671 --> 00:06:35.660
(tech music)

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.800
- [Narrator] So while XPENG hordes

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.510
it's self-driving capabilities,

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:40.820
engineers are beefing
up other tech features

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.906
like it's voice recognition system.

00:06:42.906 --> 00:06:45.489
(woman speaking foreign language)

00:06:45.489 --> 00:06:46.810
(car answers in foreign language)

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:48.810
- [Narrator] Or making its
battery management software

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.400
super efficient.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.080
XPENG has already started
selling cars in Norway

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.930
and says these tweaks will help it crack

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.590
the larger Europe market.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:07:00.310
And someday, the company plans
to have its cars on US roads

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.662
right alongside Tesla vehicles.

00:07:02.662 --> 00:07:05.339
(innovative music)

